vendor/scrcpy-server-v4.1-agent-eye.jar is the scrcpy server, version 4.1,
copyright Genymobile, licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy), modified for Agent Eye.
It is pushed to the phone to read the camera over adb. Agent Eye talks to it
directly and does not need scrcpy installed.

Modifications (vendor/scrcpy-camera-controls.patch, applied to tag v4.1;
scripts/build-server.sh rebuilds the jar):
- camera_focus=<diopters>: autofocus off, lens held at a fixed distance.
- camera_ae_lock / camera_awb_lock: lock auto exposure / white balance once
  they have settled (camera_lock_delay_ms, default 1500 ms).
- camera_3a_report: about twice a second, one log line with the lens focus
  distance (and its range over every frame since the last line), autofocus,
  exposure and white balance state.
- camera_af_region=x,y,w,h: autofocus on a part of the picture.
- camera_commands: commands on stdin change the running camera without
  restarting it (zoom, focus, af_region, af_scan, ae_lock, awb_lock).
- The 3A reports also give the zoom and the lens in use (logical cameras).
- Camera ids the list hides can be opened, and list_cameras also prints hidden
  logical multi-cameras with their lenses (zoom, nearest focus), each camera's
  manual focus range, AF regions and 3A locks.
The server protocol is unchanged.
